  'ZachXBT Exposes Axiom Exchange Insider Trading Scandal: Employee Tracked User Wallets for Profit',
  'On February 26, 2026, blockchain investigator ZachXBT published an explosive thread alleging that Axiom Exchange employees—including senior BD Broox Bauer (@WheresBroox)—abused internal dashboard access to track private user wallet addresses, UIDs, and referral codes for insider trading since early 2025. In leaked audio recordings, Bauer allegedly claimed he could "track any Axiom user" and "find out anything to do with that person," describing how he researched 10-20 wallets at a time "so it does not look that suspicious." ZachXBT''s investigation, conducted as an independent retained consultant, revealed a coordinated group sharing KOL wallet data via Google Sheets to front-run meme coin trades. Evidence included screenshots of internal lookups on prominent traders like ''Jerry'' and ''Monix,'' wallet clusters linked to the scheme, and plans for a $200K profit-sharing arrangement with moderator ''Gowno.'' Axiom (YC W25, $390M+ revenue) founders Cal (@cal_trading) and Mist (@mist_trading) responded they were "shocked and disappointed," immediately revoking tool access and launching an internal investigation. The scandal highlighted critical access control failures at a major exchange. ZachXBT suggested SDNY prosecution given Bauer''s NYC location. The expose dominated Crypto Twitter, with @tier1haterr amplifying allegations about Axiom founders'' past controversies and @Cointelegraph reporting Axiom''s damage control response. As one commenter noted: peak CT irony when the insider trading investigation itself spawned a Polymarket prediction market that became its own insider trading scandal the next day.',
